# A bare err is data, and `+` wants a value. `steeped` answers an err on one
# arm, so its answer can be one, and the operator has no arm to name it with.
# Ruled 2026-09-15: a program that hands a raised err to an operator does not
# compile; it dispatches on the answer first, the way it would on a none.
fn steeped 0
  err "nothing steeped"

fn steeped n
  n

total = steeped 0 + 1

pub play = print "{total}"
